    "result_text": "Both acceptance tests pass. Here's a summary of the full-stack change I implemented.\n\n## What changed\n\nInvoices are now **itemised** \u2014 instead of typing one figure, you list line items (description, quantity, unit price) and the amount is the sum of `qty \u00d7 unit price` across them.\n\n**Database** (`src/main/resources/db/migration/V15__line_items.sql`)\n- New `line_item` table (`invoice_id` FK, `description`, `qty`, `unit_price`).\n- Dropped the `invoice_amount_positive` check \u2014 an itemised invoice with no lines yet totals zero. The invoice's `amount` column is now a derived total, kept in step by the write paths.\n\n**Server** (OfficeFloor REST + Spring beans)\n- `LineItem` entity, `LineItemRepository`, `NewLineItem` request body.\n- `GET /api/lineitems` (`LineItemsGet`) \u2014 lists all line items; the UI scopes to one invoice.\n- `POST /api/lineitems` (`LineItemsPost`) \u2014 validates and adds a line, recomputes and stores the invoice's derived `amount`, and records `LINE_ITEM_ADDED \u2026` through the `Audit` service.\n- Two new YAML wirings under `rest/api/`.\n- `TestSupportController`: added `line_item` to the reset list (child-first) and taught the invoice seed to insert nested `lineItems` and compute the invoice's stored amount from them (falling back to an explicit `amount` when given).\n\n**Front-end** (new files only, plus the two invoice-row additions)\n- `slots/defs/invoiceDetail.ts` \u2014 the invoice-detail slot region.\n- `routes/invoice.$invoiceId.tsx` \u2014 new child route at `/invoice/$invoiceId` rendering that slot.\n- `features/invoices/InvoiceLineItemsPanel.tsx` + `lineItems.slot.tsx` \u2014 the line-items table, the derived `invoice-amount` total, and the add-line form; reads `['lineItems']` via `useQuery`, writes via `useMutation` and invalidates `['lineItems']` + `['invoices']`.\n- `InvoicesPanel.tsx` \u2014 added the `invoice-open-<id>` link per row (the invoice amount there already reads the now-derived server value, so no other change was needed).\n\n`data-testid` anchors match the spec exactly (`invoice-open-<id>`, `invoice-lineitems-table`, `lineitem-row-<id>`, `lineitem-description`, `lineitem-form-{description,qty,unitprice,submit}`, `invoice-amount`). Front-end typecheck passes and `bin/e2e` runs green (2/2).",
